  "reader": "ggml-factory-signatures.cpp --layouts",
  "reader_sha256": "c2abb4669df48b6124228fc4e68668de49054712b2abde0205a6313efeb1c312",
  "format": "Original GGML graph metadata. Each S record has its signature ID, opcode, suboperation followed by the sixteen uint32 operator parameter words, output descriptor, and occupied source slots. A descriptor extends the compact type/flags/layout fields with four extents, four byte strides and the byte offset from the view source. An input may carry a same-storage relationship to its output. Each C record lists the returned tensor signature, then each scheduled graph node signature followed by its occupied source signatures, in GGML order.",
  "relation_to_verdict": "Join C rows on factory ordinal to just factory-remaining evidence. Every detailed signature projects onto the original compact signature; each case reproduces its complete original compact signature set. A graph-level verdict covers the graph as constructed.",
  "preallocation": "For each ordinal, the parsed graph-node count equals both the admitted-node count and the vTensor-only placement count in ggml-factory-placement.tsv.gz.",
  "upstream_inputs": "ggml-factory-cases.tsv.gz",
  "map": "ggml-factory-layouts.tsv.gz",
  "reproduction": "Build the existing GGML signature reader and run with --layouts. Keep S records unchanged; retain the first two and final columns of each C record. Two independent executions produced the same upstream stdout digest. The default reader still reproduces the original compact transcript byte-for-byte."
